# Afiliantka Project Guidelines

## Product Documentation

Read [`docs/PROJECT_SPEC.md`](../../docs/PROJECT_SPEC.md) and [`ROADMAP.md`](../../ROADMAP.md) before implementing product behavior.

## Architecture

- Public website: `WEB_HOST`, route group `app/(website)/`
- Authenticated app: `APP_HOST`, route group `app/(app)/`
- Host routing is handled in `middleware.ts`.
- Do not create routes outside these groups except `app/layout.tsx` and `app/globals.css`.

## Code Style

- No `console.log` — use `console.error` only in catch blocks for real errors
- No `any` type — use proper types or `unknown` with type guards
- No unused imports or variables
- Polish for all user-facing text
- No comments that just narrate what code does — only explain non-obvious intent
- Always guard against `null`/`undefined` from external APIs before property access
- Use `"use client"` only when the component needs browser APIs or interactivity

## Mandatory gates

- Follow the multi-agent workflow and PR contract in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).
- Every behavioral change requires tests; pure docs/copy must state **Tests: N/A**.
- Never commit secrets or expose service-role credentials to the client.
- Frontend detail: [`frontend.mdc`](./frontend.mdc) and [the frontend UI skill](../skills/frontend-ui/SKILL.md).
- Backend detail: [`backend.mdc`](./backend.mdc).
- Test detail: [`testing.mdc`](./testing.mdc).
